malcolmr.google@cse.unsw.edu.au (Malcolm Ryan) writes:
> The thing that has got me confused is the "xyflags" variable in
> migrate_to_level()  and mon_arrive() in dogs.c. It appears that if the
> monster's destination level is "up" then xyflags = 1, and if we are
> currently in the wizards tower, another bit is also set. This value is
> then copied into mtmp->mtrack[0].y until the monster is revived.
> 
> In mon_arrive() xyflags is copied out of mtrack[0] and into mtmp->my.
> After that, I cannot trace it being used anywhere else.
> 
> Can anyone explain what this value is for?

It's used in rloc_pos_ok() to find which way the monster was going
and whether the Tower constraints need to be observed, so that
the correct arrival zones can be chosen. See the comments at the
head of that function.

